{"pageid":2799,"title":"Flowering Meadows","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Flowering Meadows</span>","revid":21010,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-wikia pi-layout-default type-wood\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"title1\">Flowering Meadows</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"pi-item pi-image\" data-source=\"image1\">\n\t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/1/18/Revamped_Flowering_Meadows.png/revision/latest?cb=20260104040557\" class=\"image image-thumbnail\" title=\"Revamped Flowering Meadows\">\n\t\t<img src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/1/18/Revamped_Flowering_Meadows.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/268?cb=20260104040557\" srcset=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/1/18/Revamped_Flowering_Meadows.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/268?cb=20260104040557 1x, https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/1/18/Revamped_Flowering_Meadows.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/536?cb=20260104040557 2x\" class=\"pi-image-thumbnail\" data-relevant=\"1\" alt=\"Revamped Flowering Meadows\" width=\"270\" height=\"132\" data-image-key=\"Revamped_Flowering_Meadows.png\" data-image-name=\"Revamped Flowering Meadows.png\" />\n\t\t\n\t</a>\n\t\n</figure>\n\n\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-panel pi-border-color wds-tabber\">\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tabs__wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t<ul class=\"wds-tabs\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wds-tabs__tab wds-is-current\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tabs__tab-label\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStats\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wds-tabs__tab\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tabs__tab-label\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tInfo\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content wds-is-current\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Island\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Finlay\" title=\"Finlay\">Finlay</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"NPC\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">NPC</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Laura\" title=\"Laura\">Laura</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Purpose\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Purpose</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Flowers, Dye Machine/Press Machine, Trees, Ores, Butterflies, <a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Version Added\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">1.54.0</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">April 14th, 2024</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><br />\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The Flowering Meadows is a subregion located in <a href=\"/wiki/Finlay_Island\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Finlay Island\">Finlay Island</a>. It is located to the left of Finlay's beach, and behind the <a href=\"/wiki/Resource_Hub\" title=\"Resource Hub\">Resource Hub</a>. It requires explosives, two <a href=\"/wiki/Small_Bomb\" title=\"Small Bomb\">Small Bombs</a> to be exact to enter. There is a entrance on the other side of <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Flowering Meadows</strong> that doesn't need any explosives to enter.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Stores_and_Locations\">Stores and Locations</span></h2>\n<p>The Flowering Meadows contains only one shop, called <a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a>.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a> is a shop that mainly sells items that relate to Flowers, such as the <a href=\"/wiki/Dye_Machine\" title=\"Dye Machine\">Dye Machine</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Press_Machine\" title=\"Press Machine\">Press Machine</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Jar\" title=\"Jar\">Jars</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Fabric_Roll\" title=\"Fabric Roll\">Fabric Rolls,</a> etc. The also contains the four towers required to obtain the <a href=\"/wiki/Petalfall\" title=\"Petalfall\">Petalfall Axe</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Species_of_Trees\">Species of Trees</span></h2>\n<p>The Flowering Meadows contain many different types of trees, most notably <a href=\"/wiki/Sakura\" title=\"Sakura\">Sakura</a> trees, but it also contains <a href=\"/wiki/Birch\" title=\"Birch\">Birch</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">Oak</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Willow\" title=\"Willow\">Willow</a> trees and uniquely the <a href=\"/wiki/Olivine_Clover\" title=\"Olivine Clover\">Olivine Clover</a>.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Sakura\" title=\"Sakura\">Sakura</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Willow\" title=\"Willow\">Willow</a> trees are more efficient ways to earn money, as they sell more money than the beginner trees.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mining\">Mining</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Common_Ores\">Common Ores</span></h3>\n<p>The Flowering Meadows contain many different stone nodes, such as the <a href=\"/wiki/Lightslate\" title=\"Lightslate\">Lightslate</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Beigeslate\" title=\"Beigeslate\">Beigeslate</a> nodes but also contain <a href=\"/wiki/Marble\" title=\"Marble\">Marble</a> nodes on the higher parts of the Flowering Meadows, around <a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a>.\n</p><p>In addition, many different common ores spawn in the Flowering Meadows, such as <a href=\"/wiki/Inkstone\" title=\"Inkstone\">Inkstone</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Copper\" title=\"Copper\">Copper</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Tin\" title=\"Tin\">Tin</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Pyrite\" title=\"Pyrite\">Pyrite</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">Iron</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">Gold</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Rose_Gold\" title=\"Rose Gold\">Rose Gold</a> and exclusive to <a href=\"/wiki/Marble\" title=\"Marble\">Marble</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Quartz\" title=\"Quartz\">Quartz</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rare_Ores\">Rare Ores</span></h3>\n<p>Rare Ores can spawn in the Flowering Meadows as well, such as <a href=\"/wiki/Rosa_Flama_Quartz\" title=\"Rosa Flama Quartz\">Rosa Flama Quartz</a> being exclusive to <a href=\"/wiki/Marble\" title=\"Marble\">Marble</a> nodes. The Flowering Meadows can also contain <a href=\"/wiki/Adurite\" title=\"Adurite\">Adurite</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Mythril\" title=\"Mythril\">Mythril</a>and <a href=\"/wiki/Magnetite\" title=\"Magnetite\">Magnetite</a>, which is exclusive to <a href=\"/wiki/Lightslate\" title=\"Lightslate\">Lightslate</a> and only spawns at night (assumption).\n</p><p><b>New Ores</b>\n</p><p>Amethyst ore can be found in marble stones. Amethyst ore looks like small purple crystals in marble. Also, you can see the blue stones from bloomite, this ore looks like little blue flowers.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Flowers.2FFruits\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Flowers/Fruits\">Flowers/Fruits</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Flowers\">Flowers</span></h3>\n<p>Tulips are flowers that are the only and exclusive to the Flowering Meadows. These consist of <a href=\"/wiki/Red_Tulip\" title=\"Red Tulip\">Red</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Orange_Tulip\" title=\"Orange Tulip\">Orange</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Green_Tulip\" title=\"Green Tulip\">Green</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Blue_Tulip\" title=\"Blue Tulip\">Blue</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Purple_Tulip\" title=\"Purple Tulip\">Purple</a> tulips. These flowers are also sold at <a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a>.\n</p><p>Previously mentioned, <a href=\"/wiki/Flora_Laura\" title=\"Flora Laura\">Flora Laura</a> also contains flowers that you can buy. They are the previously mentioned tulips, <a href=\"/wiki/Sunflower\" title=\"Sunflower\">Sunflowers</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Daisy\" title=\"Daisy\">Daisies</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Rose\" title=\"Rose\">Roses</a>. You can also buy already dyed tulips in a <a href=\"/wiki/Jar\" title=\"Jar\">Jar</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fruits\">Fruits</span></h3>\n<p>Only one type of <a href=\"/wiki/Fruits\" title=\"Fruits\">Fruit</a> can be found in the bushes of the Flowering Meadows, being the <a href=\"/wiki/Blueberries\" title=\"Blueberries\">Blueberry</a>. You can also find fruits in the trees of the Flowering Meadows, such as <a href=\"/wiki/Pear\" title=\"Pear\">Pears</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Apple\" title=\"Apple\">Apples</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Golden_Apple\" title=\"Golden Apple\">Golden Apples</a> (assumption)\n</p>\n<table class=\"navbox mw-collapsible\" style=\"background:#291F1D; width:100%; padding:.1em; margin:.5em auto; -webkit-border-radius:5px; -moz-border-radius:0 10px 10px 0\" data-expandtext=\"Open\" data-collapsetext=\"Close\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"width:105px; background:#140401; -webkit-border-radius:5px; -moz-border-radius:0 10px 10px 0\"><span style=\"float:left; padding-left:10px; padding-top:4px; font-size:90%\"><a href=\"/wiki/Template:Lo